class.description:
[CgameNetSchema] is built from a [Dictionary] of the form [code]{"fields": [field, ...]}[/code]. Each field is a [Dictionary] with the keys [code]name[/code], [code]type[/code] ([code]"int"[/code], [code]"float"[/code], [code]"vec3"[/code], [code]"quat"[/code], [code]"bool"[/code], [code]"string"[/code] or [code]"enum"[/code]), [code]bits[/code], [code]min[/code], [code]max[/code] and [code]condition[/code]. Use [method make_field] to build entries.
Conditions: [code]"always"[/code] sends the field in every packet; [code]"on_change"[/code] sends it when its quantized value differs from the baseline (or the baseline lacks it); [code]"initial_only"[/code] sends it only when the baseline lacks it; [code]"owner_only"[/code] is delta-coded like [code]on_change[/code] but is skipped when [code]is_owner[/code] is [code]false[/code].
Wire layout: one mask bit per schema field, then the present fields in schema order, packed LSB first. Integers and enums are stored as [code]value - min[/code] clamped to [code]bits[/code] bits; floats and vectors are fixed-point over [code][min, max][/code]; quaternions use four components over [code][-1, 1][/code]; strings use an 8-bit length and UTF-8 bytes; booleans use one bit. This is byte-compatible with the GDScript [code]net_schema.gd[/code] implementation, including [method get_schema_hash].
[codeblock]
var schema := CgameNetSchema.new()
schema.set_schema({"fields": [
    CgameNetSchema.make_field("hp", "int", 8, 0, 255),
    CgameNetSchema.make_field("pos", "vec3", 16, -512, 512),
]})
var bytes := schema.serialize({"hp": 70, "pos": Vector3(1, 2, 3)}, baseline, true)
var state := schema.deserialize(bytes, baseline)
[/codeblock]
